# EVERY env file, not just .env. Two backups I made while debugging the portal
# login (.env.backup, .env.bak2) sat here untracked with live tokens in them —
# one "git add -A" and they were public. The example file is the exception.
.env
.env.backup
.env.bak2
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local scratch / API dumps — these contain REAL Dealer Portal tokens and
# login responses. Never commit them.
dp_token.txt
dp_login.json
ep_out.json
dash.json
part.json
openapi.json

# WhatsApp linked-device leftovers (not used by the Cloud API transport)
.wwebjs_cache/
.wwebjs_auth/

*.log

# Live API response dumps captured while debugging. No credentials, but they
# carry real user/dealer ids and customer data.
analyze_sample.json
*_sample.json
*.dump.json

# Chat exports and anything replayed from them — real customer conversations.
chats/
exports/
*.zip
